{
  "name": "schema_version_gating",
  "description": "ADR-009 buffer-then-release. An event tagged with a schema_version ahead of the client's active version is buffered, not applied; a later schema refresh that raises the active version past it releases the event, and only then does it fold into the projection. The `gating` block drives both parity runners: events arrive across phases, each phase fixes the active schema version (monotonic), and events gate-then-fold accordingly. seq=3 is tagged schema_version 3 and the final active version is only 2, so it stays buffered forever — its mutation (asset bbbb...) is deliberately ABSENT from expected_projection, which is what makes this scenario actually distinguish correct gating from always-apply (HLC-LWW alone can't, since apply-order is irrelevant). The expected_projection is the state after the final phase.",
